Kubernetes Metrics Pipeline on AWS EKS: Prometheus, Thanos, S3, and Grafana

Your diagram shows a high-availability metrics pipeline. Prometheus scrapes the /metrics endpoints of your services. Two Prometheus replicas run side by side, each with a Thanos sidecar that exposes its local data and uploads 2-hour blocks to S3. Thanos Query fans out across the sidecars and the Store Gateway, deduplicates the replica data, and serves one unified view to Grafana. The Store Gateway serves historical data from S3, so you can keep months of metrics without keeping them on local disk.

This guide uses the region from your earlier work, ap-south-1 (Mumbai). Adjust it if needed.

Phase 0: Prerequisites and environment

Install these tools on your workstation:

AWS CLI v2, configured with an IAM user or SSO profile that has admin-level rights for this lab
eksctl (0.200 or later)
kubectl matching your cluster version (within one minor version)
Helm 3.14 or later
jq and git

